%% Billing plans — how a plan reaches the payment processor, and which fields are then fixed.
%% Core owns the idempotency key and the write-back; the adapter only talks to the processor.
flowchart TD
  S[Steward opens New plan] --> M{Mode}
  M -->|Create in processor| C1[Choose new product or an existing one<br/>options fetched live: lookup products]
  C1 --> C2[Currency and interval: lookup currencies, intervals<br/>amount typed]
  C2 --> SAVE[Plan saved: sync_status pending<br/>price id empty]
  M -->|Link existing price| L1[Choose a price<br/>lookup prices, narrowed by product]
  L1 --> L2[adapter.fetch_price copies amount,<br/>currency, interval and product<br/>whatever was typed]
  L2 --> L3{Found and active?}
  L3 -->|No| ERR[Rejected on the price field:<br/>not found, archived, or processor unreachable]
  L3 -->|Yes| SYNCED[Plan saved: sync_status synced<br/>nothing to push]
  SAVE --> AC[after_commit: SyncPlanJob<br/>billing queue, plan id only]
  AC --> CTX[Core builds the platform's ProcessorContext<br/>and the idempotency key]
  CTX --> SP[adapter.sync_plan context, plan, idempotency_key]
  SP --> R{Result}
  R -->|PlanSyncResult| W[Core stores product id, price id,<br/>sync_status synced via update_columns]
  W --> NOLOOP[No callbacks run, so the change is not pushed back]
  R -->|error| RT[ActiveJob retries with growing waits]
  RT --> SP
  RT -->|attempts exhausted| F[sync_status failed<br/>sync_error: short code]
  F --> RB[Steward presses Retry sync<br/>restart_sync! and enqueue again]
  RB --> AC
  SYNCED --> LOCK
  W --> LOCK[Plan is linked: fields the adapter declares create_only<br/>are locked in the form, the permitted params and validation]
  LOCK --> CP[Change price: a new plan prefilled from this one,<br/>sharing its product; the old price is untouched]
  LOCK --> SNAP[Show page: live snapshot via fetch_price and fetch_product<br/>drift flagged, cached 30 seconds]
